<jupyter_text>
The assertion checks that the sum of squares of numbers in the list (or array) equals to 1. This makes sense, because in general, the idea that this sum of squares equals 1 is used in the context of quadratic optimization problems. This assertion is crucial to understand the meaning and meaningfulness of values/numbers in the list.This feature of quadratic optimization has nothing to do with the performance of these algorithms, but helps to make our implementation more meaningful and understandable to others.
